xhale  round your spine up towards to the  ceiling tuck your chin towards your  chest releasing the tension from the  neck on the inhale arch your back lift  your head and tailbone up towards the  sky  this helps to release the tension from  the hips and back hip bridge lie with  your back and both feet flat on the  floor slowly draw your abdominals up  toward the ceiling squeezing your glutes  right at the top for five seconds  release back to stuffy position and  repeat this exercise will strengthen the  glute muscles and to release tension  from the lower back another basic  exercise to perform is abdominal  crunches which will help to strengthen  the core muscles lie on your back with  both feet flat on the floor slowly  crunch up by lifting your shoulders off  the floor hold for two seconds  Lowestoft back down and repeat thoracic  kyphosis or hunched back you have  rounded shoulders the joints of your  collarbone and breastbone are unstable  in order to stabilize this joint your  body recruits the pectoris muscles by  bringing the shoulders forward when your  shoulders are constantly pulled forward  the muscles in your back become  lengthened and weak and your chest  muscles are tight this can be caused by  sitting with a bad posture or hunched  over a computer for an extended period  of time  the first exercise is simply to be aware  and correct your posture by drawing both  shoulders down and bringing them back to  open up your chest this is the neutral  position you should be in next exercise  chest open to stretch your chest place  both hands at the back of your head  squeeze your shoulder blades together to  create tension in the upper back and  shoulders while opening up at the chest  hold this position for 10 seconds  release and repeat five times you can  even do this while sitting at a desk  Bert dark start on all fours in a  neutral position keeping your back flat  and pelvis still reach your right arm  forward and left leg back don't let your  hips 